title: Microsoft Intune: Apple MDM Push Certificate
agents: special
catalog: cloud/microsoft
license: GPLv2
distribution: Christopher Pommer
description:
 This check monitors the expiration status of the Apple MDM Push Certificate
 configured in Microsoft Intune.

 The check processes data collected by the {Microsoft Intune} special agent,
 which queries the Microsoft Graph API to retrieve the MDM push certificate
 information from the Intune tenant.

 The certificate must be renewed annually to maintain iOS, iPadOS, and macOS
 device management functionality. The service monitors remaining time until
 expiration and uses configurable thresholds to alert administrators before
 the certificate expires.

 Default mapping:

 {OK}: Certificate expires in more than 14 days

 {WARN}: Certificate expires within 14 days

 {CRIT}: Certificate expires within 5 days

 For expired certificates, the service continues to report critical state and
 displays the expiration timespan as "X ago" format.

 The service details include the certificate expiration time and the associated
 Apple ID used for certificate management.

 You must configure the {Microsoft Intune} special agent to collect Apple MDM
 Push Certificate data from your Intune tenant.

discovery:
 One service named "Intune Apple MDM push certificate" is created automatically
 if an Apple MDM Push Certificate is configured in the Intune tenant.